[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The board app hard-codes nothing the grammar can say

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-BOARD-GRAMMAR-DRIVEN
TITLE: The board app hard-codes nothing the grammar can say
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The board app SHALL contain minimal hard-coded knowledge of the system it
renders: anything the app cannot infer from the grammar is a gap. The one
permitted exception is coloring and styles, which SHALL be deterministically
validated as complete against the grammar -- every element and role styled,
none silently falling to a default -- and should ideally be literally a CSS
sheet.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Hedged by the operator -- verbatim: "one requirement I have we could add is
board (app) should contain minimal hard coded info about the system." Filed
as a REQUIREMENT node at sketch rather than parked as a work item; that
filing (and this node's continued existence) is the carver's resolution of
"we could add", reversible at grooming. Known standing violations to burn
down: TYPE_COLORS in card.js and the duplicated series colors in theme.css
(hard-coded, no completeness check); the Perspective default column lists.
<<<
